A gardener has $64$ m of fencing for three sides of a rectangular garden. An existing wall forms the fourth side. The side parallel to the wall is $x$ m long; each perpendicular side is $y$ m long.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (-0.4,2) -- (4.4,2);
\draw (0,2) -- (0,0) -- (4,0) -- (4,2);
\path (2,2) node[above] {wall};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$x$ m};
\path (0,1) node[left] {$y$ m};
\path (4,1) node[right] {$y$ m};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write the area $A$ as a function of $x$, and state the domain.

A poster has $120$ cm$^{2}$ of printed material. Its margins are $2$ cm at each side and $3$ cm at the top and bottom. The printed width is $x$ cm and printed height is $y$ cm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,5);
\draw (0.6,0.9) rectangle (3.4,4.1);
\path (2,0.9) node[above] {$x$ cm};
\path (3.4,2.5) node[left] {$y$ cm};
\path (0.3,2.5) node[rotate=90] {$2$ cm};
\path (3.7,2.5) node[rotate=90] {$2$ cm};
\path (2,0.45) node {$3$ cm};
\path (2,4.55) node {$3$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write the total poster area $A$ as a function of $x$, and state the domain.

An open box is made from an $18$ cm by $12$ cm sheet by cutting a square of side $x$ cm from each corner and folding up the sides.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.5,3);
\draw[dashed] (0.6,0) -- (0.6,3);
\draw[dashed] (3.9,0) -- (3.9,3);
\draw[dashed] (0,0.6) -- (4.5,0.6);
\draw[dashed] (0,2.4) -- (4.5,2.4);
\path (2.25,0) node[below] {$18$ cm};
\path (4.5,1.5) node[right] {$12$ cm};
\path (0,2.7) node[left] {$x$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write the volume $V$ as a function of $x$, and state the domain for a non-degenerate box.

A gutter is made from a $32$ cm wide metal strip. A strip of width $x$ cm along each edge is bent up at a right angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,1.4) -- (0,0) -- (4,0) -- (4,1.4);
\draw (0,0.2) -- (0.2,0.2) -- (0.2,0);
\draw (3.8,0) -- (3.8,0.2) -- (4,0.2);
\path (0,0.7) node[left] {$x$ cm};
\path (4,0.7) node[right] {$x$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write the cross-sectional area $A$ as a function of $x$, and state the domain.

A cylinder stands inside a cone of height $30$ cm and base radius $12$ cm. Its base lies in the cone's base plane and its top rim touches the cone. The cylinder has radius $r$ cm and height $h$ cm.
The diagram shows an axial cross-section.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2,0) -- (0,5) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw (-1.2,0) -- (-1.2,2) -- (1.2,2) -- (1.2,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (0,5);
\draw (0,2) -- (1.2,2);
\draw (0,2.2) -- (0.2,2.2) -- (0.2,2);
\path (0.6,2) node[above] {$r$ cm};
\path (1.2,1) node[left] {$h$ cm};
\draw[<->] (-2.6,0) -- (-2.6,5);
\path (-2.6,2.5) node[left] {$30$ cm};
\draw[<->] (0,-0.6) -- (2,-0.6);
\path (1,-0.6) node[below] {$12$ cm};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use corresponding-side ratios to write the cylinder's volume $V$ as a function of $r$, and state the domain.

A rectangle is inscribed in a semicircle of radius $8$ cm, with its base on the diameter and centred at the circle's centre. Its width is $2x$ cm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0);
\draw (2.5,0) arc (0:180:2.5);
\draw (-1.5,0) -- (-1.5,2) -- (1.5,2) -- (1.5,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1pt);
\draw (0,0) -- (1.5,2);
\path (0.75,1) node[above left] {$8$ cm};
\path (0,0) node[below=5mm] {$2x$ cm wide};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write the rectangle's area $A$ as a function of $x$, and state the domain.

A person rows across a river $800$ m wide, then walks along the opposite bank to a destination $6$ km downstream from the point directly opposite the start. Rowing speed is $3$ km/h and walking speed is $5$ km/h. The landing point is $x$ km downstream, where $0\leq x\leq6$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) -- (5,0);
\draw (0,2) -- (5,2);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (0,2);
\draw (0,0) -- (2,2);
\fill (0,0) circle (1pt);
\fill (2,2) circle (1pt);
\fill (5,2) circle (1pt);
\path (0,0) node[below] {start};
\path (2,2) node[above] {landing};
\path (5,2) node[right] {destination};
\path (0,1) node[left] {$800$ m};
\path (1,2) node[below] {$x$ km};
\draw[<->] (0,2.8) -- (5,2.8);
\path (2.5,2.8) node[above] {$6$ km};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write the total journey time $T$ in hours as a function of $x$.
